Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 07:56:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 3222 mpr: MultinetGetConnectionPerformance through the
 providers, LPT port selection for printer connections

MultinetGetConnectionPerformanceA/W returned WN_NO_NETWORK always. They now
resolve a redirected device with WNetGetConnection (or take lpRemoteName), ask
the named provider or each provider's NPGetConnectionPerformance and return the
documented codes (ERROR_INVALID_ADDRESS, ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER for a wrong
cbStructure, ERROR_BAD_DEVICE, ERROR_NOT_CONNECTED, ERROR_BAD_NET_NAME,
ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED, ERROR_BAD_PROVIDER, ERROR_NO_NETWORK).

WNetUseConnection with CONNECT_REDIRECT and no local name for a printer picks
the first unused LPT port (and goes on with the next while the provider says it
is taken), and a printer connection made with CONNECT_UPDATE_PROFILE is
remembered under HKCU\Network\LPTn and enumerated by RESOURCE_REMEMBERED with
"LPTn:" as its local name.

